<h1 align="center">Network Troubleshooting Report</h1>

<hr>

<h2>Case 1 – VTY Remote Access Configuration (SW-2)</h2>

<h3>Issue</h3>
<p>VTY lines required authentication configuration for secure Telnet access.</p>

<h3>Initial Configuration</h3>

```console
SW-2#show running-config | section line
line con 0
line vty 0 4
 login
line vty 5 15
 login
```

<h3>Corrective Action</h3>

```console
SW-2(config)#username netadmin secret salamaleikum
SW-2(config)#line vty 0 4
SW-2(config-line)#login local
SW-2(config-line)#end
SW-2#copy running-config startup-config
```

<h3>Verification Output</h3>

```console
C:\>telnet 192.168.10.99
Trying 192.168.10.99 ...Open

User Access Verification
Username: netadmin
Password:
SW-2>
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Remote access secured and operational.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Case 2 – VLAN 10 Missing & Trunk Restriction (SW-1)</h2>

<h3>Issue</h3>
<ul>
<li>VLAN 10 missing on SW-1</li>
<li>Fa0/2 assigned to VLAN 1</li>
<li>Trunk not allowing VLAN 10</li>
</ul>

<h3>Corrective Action</h3>

```console
SW-1(config)#interface fa0/2
SW-1(config-if)#switchport mode access
SW-1(config-if)#switchport access vlan 10

SW-1(config)#interface gig0/1
SW-1(config-if)#switchport mode trunk
SW-1(config-if)#switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30
```

<h3>Verification</h3>

```console
SW-1#show vlan brief
VLAN 10 active    Fa0/2
```

```console
SW-1#show interface trunk
Vlans allowed on trunk
Gig0/1  10,20,30
```

```console
C:\>ping 192.168.10.100
Reply from 192.168.10.100: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=128
Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 4, Lost = 0 (0% loss)
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> VLAN segmentation corrected and connectivity restored.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Case 3 – SW-0 Fa0/1 Unconfigured</h2>

<h3>Corrective Action</h3>

```console
SW-0(config)#interface fa0/1
SW-0(config-if)#switchport mode access
SW-0(config-if)#switchport access vlan 20
SW-0#copy running-config startup-config
```

<h3>Verification</h3>

```console
SW-0#show vlan brief
20   VLAN0020   active   Fa0/1, Fa0/2
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Port assigned correctly to VLAN 20.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Case 4 – Unused Ports Shutdown (Security Hardening)</h2>

```console
SW-0(config)#interface range fa0/4 - 24
SW-0(config-if-range)#shutdown

SW-2(config)#interface range fa0/2 - 24
SW-2(config-if-range)#shutdown
```

```console
%LINK-5-CHANGED: Interface FastEthernet0/4, changed state to administratively down
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Unused interfaces administratively disabled.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Case 5 – Unused Ports Assigned to VLAN 99 (SW-2)</h2>

```console
SW-2(config)#interface range fa0/2 - 24
SW-2(config-if-range)#switchport mode access
SW-2(config-if-range)#switchport access vlan 99
```

```console
% Access VLAN does not exist. Creating vlan 99
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Default VLAN exposure reduced.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Case 6 – Incorrect VLAN Assignment (SW-1 Fa0/1)</h2>

```console
SW-1(config)#interface fa0/1
SW-1(config-if)#switchport mode access
SW-1(config-if)#switchport access vlan 30
SW-1#copy running-config startup-config
```

```console
C:\>ping 192.168.30.102
Reply from 192.168.30.102: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=128
Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 4, Lost = 0 (0% loss)
```

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Correct VLAN segmentation restored. Connectivity verified.</p>

